# Clone can't copy a creature entering at the same time as it (the card's ruling, CR 614.1c, 707.2), so when the only
# other creature is one entering with it there is nothing to copy and nothing is asked. Bot1's Clone dies as a 0/0 on
# turn 1 with no creature to copy; Bot2 discards a Guerrilla Gorilla to hand size on turn 2. On turn 3 Exhume returns
# Clone and the Gorilla together: Bot1 is not asked whether to copy ("! Bot1.Accept"), and the Clone, a 0/0 again, goes
# back to the graveyard after Exhume (CR 704.5f). The Gorilla stays. The positive control is
# clone-returned-by-exhume-cannot-copy-a-creature-entering-with-it, where an Ornithopter is already out and it is asked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Clone
Island
Island
Exhume
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Guerrilla Gorilla x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Clone.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Clone; Black Lotus
? Bot2.Graveyard = Guerrilla Gorilla
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Exhume.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet
Bot1.Graveyard = Clone; Exhume; Black Lotus
Bot2.Battlefield = Guerrilla Gorilla
